<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<suite name="mam_wetdep" version="1.0">
  <!--
    Standalone validation suite for MAM aerosol wet deposition: convective
    processing (aero_convproc: in-updraft transport, activation, wet removal,
    resuspension) followed by stratiform scavenging (wetdepa_v2 in the
    aero_wetdep_ccpp orchestration).  See design_docs mam_project_scratchpad
    wetdep_ccpp_plan.mono.md for the full design.

    Snapshots: classic CAM cam_snapshot around aero_model_wetdep
    (cam_take_snapshot_before/after = "aero_model_wetdep").
      ncdata       = the "before" tape: state/pbuf/cnst dumps feed every
                     input (cloud + precip fields, ZM gathered arrays via
                     pbuf_ZM_*, tphysbc_dlf, constituents incl. cloud-borne
                     via pbuf_<name>, per-constituent fracis via
                     pbuf_FRACIS_<name>). Registry reads re-inject every
                     step, so each step is an independent verdict.
      ncdata_check = the "after" tape.

    TWO CAPTURE PAIRS validate BOTH convproc paths with this ONE suite
    (runtime convproc_do_aer, aerosol_convproc_opts):
     GATE 1: convproc_do_aer=.false. capture + namelist override - convproc
             is a guarded no-op; isolates stratiform wetdepa_v2 + the
             cloud-borne in-place refactor (loop order interstitial first).
     GATE 2: convproc_do_aer=.true. capture, default namelist - convproc +
             activation live (cloud-borne phase first, resuspension
             cross-feed). Gate 1 must still pass afterward.

    Comparison surfaces (all bitwise if the port is b4b):
     - mam_wetdep_tend rows (ptend_<name>) vs CAM's ptend%q capture
       (cam_snapshot_ptend_outfld runs BEFORE physics_update, and only when
       cam_take_snapshot_before == _after - set BOTH on the capture): the
       interstitial tendencies (convproc + stratiform). PRIMARY GATE.
     - cloud-borne constituents (pbuf_<name_cw>): updated IN PLACE, matching
       CAM's qqcw writes op-for-op (physics_update does not touch pbuf).
     - fracis rows (pbuf_FRACIS_<name>): wetdepa_v2's insoluble fraction.
     - interstitial cnst_<name> rows are EXPECTED DIFFS, excluded class-based
       in the testmods: CAM's after-tape state capture runs AFTER
       physics_update, so those targets hold apply-plus-qneg3 results
       (q += ptend*dt, then qneg3 at CAM's per-constituent qmin), while this
       suite deliberately does not apply. The end state is fully determined
       by the checked tendency; reproducing it in-suite would need an apply
       + a qmin-matched qneg (production wiring, not this scheme's science).
     - untouched constituents and input registry rows: injection-integrity
       gates (before == after for everything wetdep does not write).

    Host requirements: MAM aerosol instances active (physprop namelist);
    aero_wetdep_nl + aerosol_convproc_opts namelists.

    Intentionally no qneg and no apply_constituent_tendencies (see above).
  -->

  <group name="physics_before_coupler">
    <!-- Register MAM aerosol species (interstitial + cloud-borne) as CCPP
         constituents -->
    <scheme>mam_constituents</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: mode metadata + species index maps (interstitial and
         cloud-borne constituent maps drive both wetdep schemes) -->
    <scheme>mam_mode_metadata</scheme>

    <!-- Init-only: wv_sat_init (activate_aerosol computes saturation via
         qsat inside convproc's activation) -->
    <scheme>to_be_ccppized_temporary</scheme>

    <!-- Zero the shared constituent tendencies at cluster entry (CAM:
         physics_ptend_init at every aero_wetdep_tend call). Load-bearing
         here because this suite omits apply_constituent_tendencies (the
         production zeroing point): without it steps >= 2 would accumulate
         stale tendencies. -->
    <scheme>mam_wetdep_tend_reset</scheme>

    <!-- Convective processing: deep-convective transport, activation, wet
         removal and resuspension. Accumulates interstitial tendencies into
         the shared constituent tendencies, applies evaporated-rain
         resuspension to cloud-borne constituents in place. Guarded no-op
         when convproc_do_aer=.false. Must precede aero_wetdep_ccpp (CAM
         sequences convproc before the stratiform bins loop). -->
    <scheme>aero_convproc_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=aero_convproc_run -->

    <!-- Stratiform scavenging orchestration: wetdepa_v2 over bins x phases,
         cloud-borne updated in place, interstitial tendencies accumulated,
         fracis written -->
    <scheme>aero_wetdep_ccpp</scheme><!-- dropsonde:portable=wetdepa_v2 -->

    <!-- Checkpoint the accumulated tendencies into mam_wetdep_tend
         (ptend_<name> check rows vs CAM's after-tape ptend capture) -->
    <scheme>mam_wetdep_tend_checkpoint</scheme>
  </group>
</suite>
